From 7155459be7ed10f4bc654f8b5ac24336b1144e82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josef Raschen <josef@raschen.org>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 09:35:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] net: phy: microchip_t1: restore lan887x interrupt mask
 after config_aneg

lan887x_config_aneg() issues a chip soft-reset (LAN887X_CHIP_SOFT_RST)
as required by the speed-change errata. The reset leaves all interrupts
masked and nothing re-enables them afterwards - unlike the chip
hard-reset path in lan887x_cd_reset(), which re-runs config_intr()
after resetting the chip. Reconfiguring a running interface, e.g. with
"ethtool -s ... master-slave forced-master", therefore silently
disables link-state interrupts and later link changes go unnoticed when
the PHY operates in interrupt mode.

Re-apply the interrupt configuration at the end of config_aneg().
Calling the config_intr callback directly from the driver has precedent
in micrel.c.

Fixes: 5fad1c1a09ac ("net: phy: microchip_t1: Interrupt support for lan887x")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/net/phy/microchip_t1.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/phy/microchip_t1.c b/drivers/net/phy/microchip_t1.c
index c6a2beb78325..65dc585510bf 100644
--- a/drivers/net/phy/microchip_t1.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/microchip_t1.c
@@ -1496,7 +1496,18 @@ static int lan887x_config_aneg(struct phy_device *phydev)
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
 
-	return lan887x_phy_reconfig(phydev);
+	ret = lan887x_phy_reconfig(phydev);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return ret;
+
+	/* The chip soft-reset above leaves all interrupts masked; re-apply
+	 * the interrupt configuration so link events keep being reported in
+	 * IRQ mode.
+	 */
+	if (phy_interrupt_is_valid(phydev))
+		ret = phydev->drv->config_intr(phydev);
+
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static int lan887x_probe(struct phy_device *phydev)
